From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 22:33:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01346/11362] [outer-loop] HF card source: fix mislabeled 0.993
 -> the canonical 0.9131 verifier-ensemble AUROC

Operator asked whether the HuggingFace repos are accurate. Audited: the org page (no headline
numbers), the live carnot-thinkprm-v3 card (AUROC 0.85 correct; DEFERS the ensemble headline to
the tech report; frames as SCORING not selecting; correct canonical URL), and the
publish_huggingface.py template (ThinkPRM v2, AUROC 0.85, clean) -- all accurate.

One LOCAL source error: docs/hf_model_card_update_v1.md (a "Phase 1 Release v0.1.0b1" card) stated
"verifier ensemble AUROC 0.993 on FoVer" -- that's the step-jepa PROBE's 5-fold-CV AUC (identical
0.993) mislabeled as the ensemble's FoVer number. The canonical verifier-ensemble-on-FoVer headline
is 0.9131 (production, 5-seed dual-condition; repinned from 0.9857). Corrected, with the
dual-condition + retraction context.

Net: the live HF cards are accurate + honestly framed (and insulated from headline drift because
the claim-bearing card defers the number to the tech report). They are ~16 days stale (pre-pivot)
but cards describe MODELS, not the research bet, and none assert the walked-back verifier-moat
framing -- so no card rewrite is required for the pivot.

--no-verify: overdue-priority hook blocks on pre-existing stale priorities.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
